  "rationale": "K-outer scheduling with B-tile latching: B0 and B1 are each loaded exactly once (512 bytes total for B); all 10 distinct A tiles are loaded once (2560 bytes), so DMA input is 3072 bytes, the proven minimum since every A/B tile is distinct and required. Each K-slice first computes row block i with overwrite into accumulator tile (i mod 2)*16, using preload-staged B for i==0 and the latched B tile (accumulated=true with GARBAGE preload) for i>0; the second K-slice accumulates (out_addr bit 30 set) onto the partials from slice 0, then mvouts each finished 16x16 C tile. Scratchpad holds A at row 0 and B at row 16 (both multiple of 16, within 32 rows); accumulator tiles at rows 0/16 within 32 rows. Strides: A 32 bytes, B 16 bytes, C 64 bytes per row. All out_addr/mvout acc_addr set bits 31 and 29. Expanded commands: 42. Reduction order is increasing K per output, as required."
